            <ArticleTitle>The Antigastric Cancer Activity of San Leng Powder Extract Induces Apoptosis in Balb/C Bearing-SGC-7901 Mice.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1052125</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1155/2017/1052125</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>San Leng powder extract has been used as medicinal compound for the prevention and treatment of cancers. The antitumor activity of SLPE was determined by treating BALB/C mice harboring a human gastric cancer xenograft with SPLE for 17 days. Mice were also treated with fluorouracil (5-Fu, 25 mg/kg) or a combination of SLPE and 5-Fu. Our results indicate that the inhibition of tumor growth by SLPE might be due to a block in the cell cycle and the induction of apoptosis. These results suggest that SLPE might be useful in the treatment of gastric cancer.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
